09:59 < lightlike> Moneyball: then what do you suggest should change from the status quo, where already almost everyone  uses AI locally, with a few projects doing systematic bug finding? What would be "state of the art" if the status quo isnt?
09:59 < sipa> Moneyball: are you asking what people are using? trying to encourage some kind of usage? better documenting? 
09:59 < Moneyball> sipa i was asked to come here to raise this topic. i'm merely asking "what content can be shared with inquiring minds about how the Core project isn't behind the times on utilizing AI." i have never brought up the topic of "you must use a review bot in github" that is made up.
09:59 < andrewtoth> that was me bringing up it was a bad idea, sorry for the noise
09:59 < Moneyball> andrewtoth no worries
